      "idx": 0,
      "label": "1",
      "overlay": 0,
      "note": "SAY: Last time, we taught a basic Python\nroutine, but reliable helper use remained\nopen. Today adds a harder training result\nand a study of how helper answers return\nto their source records.\n\nFOCUS: Can changing the RLM's surrounding\nprogram make complete solutions more\nreliable?\n\nCAUTION: The old and new training tests\nare different tasks, not points on one\nprogress curve."
    },
    {
      "idx": 1,
      "label": "2",
      "overlay": 0,
      "note": "SAY: Follow one example. A file holds many\nusers' questions. The main model asks\nhelpers which questions concern places,\nthen Python combines those replies into\nuser totals. It can inspect the result and\ncontinue.\n\nWHY: An unfamiliar whole may become\nfamiliar smaller steps.\n\nCAUTION: This motivates RLMs; our\nexperiments do not demonstrate general\nautonomous planning or deep recursion."
    },
    {
      "idx": 2,
      "label": "3",
      "overlay": 0,
      "note": "SAY: Worked examples taught what action to\ntake next, not just the final number. On\n72 shared questions, verified successes\nwere 12 before this training and 55 or 53\nafterward.\n\nIF ASKED: Missing outcomes allow 12–19,\n55, and 53–55. The two trained copies used\ndifferent example sets, not sequential\ntraining.\n\nCAUTION: Familiar question types; the\nhelper remained fixed."
    },
    {
      "idx": 3,
      "label": "4",
      "overlay": 0,
      "note": "SAY: Maya bought a red bike. The first\nstatement is supported; the second is\ncontradicted. Repeat an arbitrary name\nbeside each statement and its answer, so\nthey can be matched explicitly.\n\nIF ASKED: Software fixed names and format,\nbut not the reading answers. The unnamed\nversion relies on list position.\n\nTRANSITION: Does this small interface\nchange matter when many questions are\nanswered together?"
    },
    {
      "idx": 4,
      "label": "5",
      "overlay": 0,
      "note": "SAY: Read left to right as each call\nhandles more questions. At 64, names\nraised Qwen from 44% to 83%, and Mistral\nfrom 35% to 52%.\n\nIF ASKED: Same 16 record sets; 160 calls\nper model shown. Three malformed Mistral\nnamed outputs count wrong, not missing.\n\nCAUTION: These are helper answers, not\ncomplete RLM solutions. Full three-format\nresults are backup 6."
    },
    {
      "idx": 5,
      "label": "6",
      "overlay": 0,
      "note": "SAY: All methods handled the same 768\nquestions. Large named calls scored 85% in\n91 seconds; single-question calls scored\n87% in 31 seconds.\n\nIF ASKED: Four calls ran concurrently,\neven for single-question requests.\nSixteen-question calls were faster but\nless accurate. Startup is excluded.\n\nCAUTION: Single-question calls sent about\n2.5 times as many input tokens as large\nnamed calls. Local speed is not universal\ncost."
    },
    {
      "idx": 6,
      "label": "7",
      "overlay": 0,
      "note": "SAY: Let the RLM program manage record-\nlevel groups and returned answers. Then\ntest complete solutions against the\ncurrent RLM and simpler small-call\nbaselines at a fixed budget.\n\nIF ASKED: Current ask_batch aligns whole\nrequests. This adds individual-record\nhandling inside requests. Learning when to\nresize groups is a later step.\n\nCAUTION: This component is proposed. IDs\nare standard, and correct matching cannot\nguarantee true reading answers."
    },
    {
      "idx": 7,
      "label": "8",
      "overlay": 0,
      "note": "SAY: Training improved a routine; matching\nnames improved helper reading. I recommend\na focused whole-task study of the handoff\nprocedure.\n\nDISCUSS: Is this a worthwhile\ncontribution? Which realistic task would\nmake a convincing test?\n\nSTOP: This ends the ten-minute main talk.\nRemaining slides are optional answers to\nquestions, not more required presentation."
    },
    {
      "idx": 8,
      "label": "9",
      "overlay": 0,
      "note": "SAY: Ada's place-question weights total\nseven; Ben's total two. Only Ada exceeds\nfive, so the answer is one user.\n\nIF ASKED: The model learns actions that\nquery helpers and calculate from their\nreal replies. Wrong helper labels can\nspoil correct arithmetic.\n\nCAUTION: These four rows are an\nillustration, not a copied training\nexample. The weights are artificial\nvalues, not confidence."
    },
    {
      "idx": 9,
      "label": "10",
      "overlay": 0,
      "note": "SAY: Both versions had names, but only one\nreused the same names on both sides.\nAccuracy on later answers rose from 32.6%\nto 78.8%, with valid formatting\nthroughout.\n\nIF ASKED: Position still specified which\nrecord to answer; different names did not\ninstruct a different task.\n\nCAUTION: Different input panel from main\nslide 5. This supports matching as a\nfactor, not an internal-mechanism claim."
    },
    {
      "idx": 10,
      "label": "11",
      "overlay": 0,
      "note": "SAY: Longer reward runs did not improve\nfinal-answer counts: 57 before, 55–57 with\nanswer reward, and 54 with an extra\ncalculation check.\n\nIF ASKED: Each attempted 576 solutions; 19\nand 21 updates actually used informative\ngroups. Together they took about four\nhours and 39 minutes.\n\nCAUTION: This scores final numbers, unlike\nslide 3. Full calculation review is\npending; it does not disprove reward\nlearning."
